    "summary": "Built the pinned CoWasm/WASI toolchain and a receipt-authenticated production package from mathematical source commit 74ce23f2c607a1cf6ac89152be6a40a3184f2bd5: 42 registered kernel families, 35 production families, 245 compiled functions, and zero unsupported production functions. The artifact now contains all 15 registered hyperelliptic Cantor, Kummer, genus-2 height, Float64 period, and genus-3 candidate functions. Added the missing Float64 result export and a checked Python numeric-to-Float64 ABI, completed the browser lazy-module closure, regenerated release capabilities and workload evidence, and added exact dynamic/direct-WASI/relocated-Node/relocated-Chromium differentials with authenticated route telemetry. Production artifact identity is sha256:8d608901aad77ca5a3bf3fe593c0fd5c576555add8676f2c65c9d964f5d0d541; kernel-flint.wasm is 5750054 bytes (sha256 8cbcc9d7cd194cd4b04c156f472597c0830b777e422727c1a50e885e99cf86c8) and kernel-gmp.wasm is 2276439 bytes (sha256 2261e4f7c5b7306a337a4dbdac707c9ff71fadd87adaadc7172f305f50c90c76). The manifest contains only canonical package-relative logical sources and excludes the desktop-only rational QQ workspace FFI.",
